# el++ engine fixture 33 (src/test.slop: test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).
# K6: a class's run reads W only where W's facts are safe. A ⊑ {a} ⊓ C puts
# C on a in W, where every class is seeded at once, but A may be empty, so
# a ∈ C is not entailed. B ⊑ ∃r.{a} with ∃r.C ⊑ D must therefore NOT give
# B ⊑ D; a run that read W's facts about a (an individual, so unsafe) would.
# Expect: A ⊑ C, and nothing for B.
# Inside el++ whole: the engine must answer every class as the literal Psc
# reference does (test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).

@prefix : <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:oneOf ( :a ) ] , :C .
:B rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom [ owl:oneOf ( :a ) ] ] .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :C ] rdfs:subClassOf :D .
